WEBVTT

1
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.480
<i>If you're wondering who you are...</i>

2
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.514
<i>you're not alone.</i>

3
00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.061
<i>You're no monkey's uncle.</i>

4
00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:31.399
<i>But you are rather peculiar.</i>

5
00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:38.656
<i>Where did you come from
and who were your ancestors?</i>

6
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.450
<i>Nope.</i>

7
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.545
<i>Guess again.</i>

8
00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:47.081
<i>That's right.</i>

9
00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:54.223
<i>The story of lemurs
begins over 60 million years ago.</i>

10
00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:57.550
<i>Back in the time of the dinosaurs.</i>

11
00:01:58.035 --> 00:02:01.929
<i>Long before monkeys, apes,
or humans ever existed.</i>

12
00:02:04.064 --> 00:02:06.946
<i>Lemurs were small nocturnal creatures</i>

13
00:02:07.046 --> 00:02:11.227
<i>and survived the asteroid
that killed the dinosaurs.</i>

14
00:02:18.514 --> 00:02:20.748
<i>They were living in Africa...</i>

15
00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:28.122
<i>when a massive storm
blew a tangled raft of trees out to sea...</i>

16
00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:32.511
<i>and turned a family of tiny lemurs...</i>

17
00:02:32.611 --> 00:02:38.341
<i>into some of the greatest explorers
in the history of life on Earth.</i>

18
00:04:45.243 --> 00:04:47.813
<i>The lemurs landed on Madagascar.</i>

19
00:04:47.913 --> 00:04:52.058
<i>A vast island isolated
from the rest of the world.</i>

20
00:04:59.341 --> 00:05:04.737
<i>For millions of years, there were
no other mammals, or even birds.</i>

21
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.086
<i>With no predators to fear...</i>

22
00:05:11.186 --> 00:05:14.747
<i>lemurs emerged into the daylight.</i>

23
00:05:15.482 --> 00:05:22.588
<i>And over time they evolved into
a wild variety of new shapes and sizes.</i>

24
00:05:29.246 --> 00:05:32.890
<i>Their ancestors went extinct in Africa.</i>

25
00:05:33.417 --> 00:05:37.520
<i>But in Madagascar, lemurs thrived...</i>

26
00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:45.277
<i>and became the rulers
of their glorious new world.</i>

27
00:06:44.696 --> 00:06:49.434
<i>Lemurs are the most ancient
primate alive today.</i>

28
00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:54.889
<i>And Madagascar is the only place
on Earth where they live.</i>

29
00:06:55.957 --> 00:07:01.738
<i>For a scientist seeking to preserve
our planet's rich biodiversity...</i>

30
00:07:01.838 --> 00:07:05.065
<i>Madagascar is Treasure Island.</i>

31
00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:16.795
<i>Dr. Patricia Wright is a primatologist
from New York's Stony Brook University.</i>

32
00:07:16.895 --> 00:07:21.790
<i>She's an expert
in finding rare and elusive lemurs.</i>

33
00:07:25.237 --> 00:07:31.467
<i>As a young scientist, her destiny
was changed by a journey to Madagascar.</i>

34
00:07:47.425 --> 00:07:50.662
<i>Back then, the country
was changing fast.</i>

35
00:07:50.762 --> 00:07:54.615
<i>And the lemurs' good luck
was running out.</i>

36
00:07:59.271 --> 00:08:03.091
<i>I first came to Madagascar
to solve a mystery...</i>

37
00:08:03.191 --> 00:08:07.503
<i>about a lemur
that we feared had gone extinct.</i>

38
00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.924
<i>My mission was to find it.</i>

39
00:08:15.245 --> 00:08:19.566
<i>The greater bamboo lemur
once lived throughout Madagascar...</i>

40
00:08:19.666 --> 00:08:23.686
<i>but hadn't been seen in 50 years.</i>

41
00:08:32.888 --> 00:08:37.616
<i>I searched for months
and never saw a single one.</i>

42
00:08:41.271 --> 00:08:45.874
<i>I had almost given up,
when I got to Ranomafana.</i>

43
00:08:47.903 --> 00:08:50.379
<i>Then one morning...</i>

44
00:08:51.531 --> 00:08:53.465
<i>there he was.</i>

45
00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:56.427
<i>Alive.</i>

46
00:08:59.414 --> 00:09:02.725
<i>Feasting on his favorite treat:</i>

47
00:09:03.585 --> 00:09:06.770
<i>Crunchy, young bamboo shoots.</i>

48
00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:32.722
<i>After her discovery...</i>

49
00:09:32.822 --> 00:09:37.435
<i>Patricia helped save this rain forest
as a national park.</i>

50
00:09:37.535 --> 00:09:42.774
<i>And she devoted her life to protecting
the wild places of Madagascar...</i>

51
00:09:42.874 --> 00:09:46.435
<i>and all the animals that call it home.</i>

52
00:09:58.431 --> 00:10:02.910
<i>The word lemur means "wandering spirit."</i>

53
00:10:05.855 --> 00:10:11.335
<i>And there is something otherworldly
about the lemurs of this forest.</i>

54
00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:18.175
<i>These lemurs are sacred in Madagascar.</i>

55
00:10:28.044 --> 00:10:32.782
<i>There is a legend about two brothers
who lived in the forest.</i>

56
00:10:32.882 --> 00:10:37.069
<i>One ran off and became the first human.</i>

57
00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:41.782
<i>The other stayed and became...</i>

58
00:10:44.227 --> 00:10:46.120
<i>an indri.</i>

59
00:10:52.736 --> 00:10:56.839
<i>There were once lemurs
as big as gorillas.</i>

60
00:10:57.198 --> 00:11:02.479
<i>But those were hunted to extinction
just a few hundred years ago.</i>

61
00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:06.515
<i>Indri are the largest lemurs
that remain.</i>

62
00:11:14.257 --> 00:11:19.027
<i>Indri live in small family groups
that have their own territories.</i>

63
00:11:22.182 --> 00:11:26.869
<i>They trade news with each other
by singing haunting duets.</i>

64
00:11:39.157 --> 00:11:42.734
<i>Each family member adds their part...</i>

65
00:11:45.205 --> 00:11:49.099
<i>to a chorus that travels
deep into the forest.</i>

66
00:12:17.112 --> 00:12:22.809
<i>The song of indri once echoed loudly
across the eastern rain forest...</i>

67
00:12:22.909 --> 00:12:25.802
<i>but now it's fading away.</i>

68
00:12:28.623 --> 00:12:32.935
<i>No indri has ever survived in captivity.</i>

69
00:12:35.505 --> 00:12:38.315
<i>You can only meet one here...</i>

70
00:12:40.135 --> 00:12:42.486
<i>in Madagascar.</i>

71
00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:42.764
<i>The town of Ranomafana is on the edge
of the ancient rainforest...</i>

72
00:13:42.864 --> 00:13:46.349
<i>where I found the greater bamboo lemurs.</i>

73
00:13:48.411 --> 00:13:53.108
<i>The people in the surrounding villages
benefit from the park.</i>

74
00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:55.902
<i>But they still rely
on the land to survive.</i>

75
00:13:59.339 --> 00:14:04.911
<i>Before I was a scientist,
I was a social worker in Brooklyn.</i>

76
00:14:05.011 --> 00:14:07.487
<i>It's my nature to solve problems.</i>

77
00:14:08.431 --> 00:14:14.254
<i>And in Madagascar,
humans and lemurs have the same problem:</i>

78
00:14:14.354 --> 00:14:18.498
<i>Limited resources that they both need.</i>

79
00:14:47.595 --> 00:14:53.075
<i>Madagascar was one of the last places
on Earth settled by humans.</i>

80
00:14:53.977 --> 00:14:57.755
<i>They brought a small breed
of cattle called zebu...</i>

81
00:14:57.855 --> 00:15:00.916
<i>that need open space for grazing.</i>

82
00:15:05.613 --> 00:15:08.850
<i>Since their arrival 2000 years ago...</i>

83
00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:14.939
<i>people have burned down
over 90 percent of Madagascar's forests...</i>

84
00:15:15.039 --> 00:15:19.434
<i>to clear land for grazing and farming.</i>

85
00:15:35.476 --> 00:15:37.712
<i>Every dry season...</i>

86
00:15:37.812 --> 00:15:42.874
<i>thousands of fires
still burn across the island.</i>

87
00:15:51.034 --> 00:15:55.396
<i>The fires are set in fields,
but grow out of control...</i>

88
00:15:55.496 --> 00:15:59.474
<i>and spread to the forests
where lemurs live.</i>

89
00:16:07.717 --> 00:16:13.029
<i>It's the biggest threat
to wildlife in Madagascar.</i>

90
00:16:34.869 --> 00:16:40.233
<i>Many lemur species are dwindling
as their forests disappear.</i>

91
00:16:40.333 --> 00:16:43.736
<i>But one crafty lemur
has bet its survival...</i>

92
00:16:43.836 --> 00:16:49.107
<i>on the ability to adapt
to changing conditions.</i>

93
00:16:53.471 --> 00:16:56.531
<i>Beyond the reach of fire...</i>

94
00:16:56.724 --> 00:17:02.704
<i>gangs of ring-tailed lemurs
have found their perfect hideout.</i>

95
00:17:26.587 --> 00:17:30.742
<i>Ring-tails live in groups
of extended families.</i>

96
00:17:30.842 --> 00:17:37.197
<i>And it's easy to observe one of the things
that makes all lemurs special among primates.</i>

97
00:17:40.935 --> 00:17:44.579
<i>The females are in charge.</i>

98
00:17:56.284 --> 00:18:01.555
<i>The alpha female decides
where they go and what they eat.</i>

99
00:18:05.334 --> 00:18:08.696
<i>This troop's leader is hobbled
by a broken hand...</i>

100
00:18:08.796 --> 00:18:12.691
<i>but that doesn't affect
her position at the top.</i>

101
00:18:21.893 --> 00:18:24.212
<i>Even the smallest female...</i>

102
00:18:24.312 --> 00:18:27.539
<i>is dominant over every male.</i>

103
00:18:37.158 --> 00:18:41.386
<i>Females inherit their power
from their mother.</i>

104
00:18:41.621 --> 00:18:46.224
<i>They keep it
through experience and attitude.</i>

105
00:19:01.474 --> 00:19:05.368
<i>Ring-tails once covered
much wider territory in Madagascar.</i>

106
00:19:06.521 --> 00:19:09.716
<i>But as humans spread out,
the ring-tails...</i>

107
00:19:09.816 --> 00:19:14.336
<i>retreated into the cracks
of this natural fortress.</i>

108
00:19:21.828 --> 00:19:23.813
<i>Like lemur outlaws...</i>

109
00:19:23.913 --> 00:19:29.976
<i>they live on the edge of civilization
and launch raids on the farms below.</i>

110
00:20:24.891 --> 00:20:30.161
<i>At night,
the day's squabbles are forgotten.</i>

111
00:20:31.689 --> 00:20:38.221
<i>The ring-tailed family grooms each other
and sleeps cuddled up in one big lemur ball.</i>

112
00:21:00.009 --> 00:21:03.862
<i>They survive by sticking together.</i>

113
00:21:32.166 --> 00:21:36.696
<i>Patricia's headquarters in Madagascar
is the Centre ValBio...</i>

114
00:21:36.796 --> 00:21:42.702
<i>a state-of-the-art research station perched
on the edge of Ranomafana National Park.</i>

115
00:21:42.802 --> 00:21:46.071
<i>Home to 15 kinds of lemurs.</i>

116
00:21:46.597 --> 00:21:49.981
<i>It's here that she's training
a new generation...</i>

117
00:21:50.081 --> 00:21:53.147
<i>of Western and Malagasy scientists...</i>

118
00:21:53.247 --> 00:21:56.581
<i>to build a future for the lemurs.</i>

119
00:21:58.442 --> 00:22:02.513
<i>Almost all the plants and animals
in Madagascar are endemic...</i>

120
00:22:02.613 --> 00:22:06.883
<i>and exist nowhere else on Earth.</i>

121
00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:12.607
<i>The more we learn
about their intricate relationships...</i>

122
00:22:12.707 --> 00:22:18.228
<i>the more we can do to protect the forest
and eventually to expand it.</i>

123
00:23:09.847 --> 00:23:15.285
<i>To the lemurs, all this science
can seem awfully mysterious.</i>

124
00:23:20.274 --> 00:23:27.297
<i>Each night, Herman and Victor set traps
in the forest around ValBio...</i>

125
00:23:27.823 --> 00:23:32.102
<i>to catch the smallest primate
in the world.</i>

126
00:23:37.833 --> 00:23:43.354
<i>To these mouse lemurs,
it's like being abducted by aliens.</i>

127
00:23:44.381 --> 00:23:49.412
<i>They're taken to a strange laboratory
and scanned, probed...</i>

128
00:23:49.512 --> 00:23:53.031
<i>and analyzed by giant creatures.</i>

129
00:23:59.063 --> 00:24:03.592
<i>They may be small,
but mouse lemurs are fierce predators...</i>

130
00:24:03.692 --> 00:24:09.547
<i>that strike terror into insects
and frogs across the galaxy.</i>

131
00:24:17.331 --> 00:24:21.517
<i>After a few hours,
the mouse lemurs are released...</i>

132
00:24:22.753 --> 00:24:29.150
<i>and head home to their nests
with an out of this world story to tell.</i>

133
00:24:49.029 --> 00:24:53.383
<i>I'm happiest when I'm alone
in the forest with lemurs.</i>

134
00:24:55.744 --> 00:25:00.223
<i>Lemurs have a very calm presence.</i>

135
00:25:03.502 --> 00:25:08.273
<i>The greater bamboo lemur
has a special place in my heart.</i>

136
00:25:08.924 --> 00:25:13.204
<i>They're not the most famous lemur,
and they're not the most beautiful...</i>

137
00:25:15.514 --> 00:25:20.952
<i>but they have this mischievous charm
that I just fell in love with.</i>

138
00:25:26.859 --> 00:25:32.297
<i>There were once millions of them,
but now they're extremely endangered.</i>

139
00:25:33.157 --> 00:25:38.845
<i>These two are the only ones living
in a protected forest.</i>

140
00:25:42.249 --> 00:25:49.073
<i>This father and his daughter have been all
alone for two years since mom disappeared.</i>

141
00:25:49.173 --> 00:25:55.361
<i>For the species to survive,
I have to help this family now.</i>

142
00:25:56.472 --> 00:26:00.459
<i>They need new mates
from outside the park.</i>

143
00:26:00.559 --> 00:26:04.829
<i>And I'll have to play lemur matchmaker.</i>

144
00:26:11.946 --> 00:26:16.142
<i>All over Madagascar,
the country's own scientists...</i>

145
00:26:16.242 --> 00:26:20.386
<i>are also working hard
to protect the lemurs.</i>

146
00:26:20.955 --> 00:26:26.235
<i>Dr. Hanta Rasamimanana works
in the spiny forest.</i>

147
00:26:26.335 --> 00:26:32.565
<i>A bizarre habitat of euphorbias
and prickly cactus-like trees.</i>

148
00:26:33.801 --> 00:26:38.571
<i>She's a census taker,
on the lookout for her favorite lemur...</i>

149
00:26:39.390 --> 00:26:41.366
<i>the sifaka.</i>

150
00:26:53.070 --> 00:26:56.506
<i>Sifaka are so curious.</i>

151
00:26:56.782 --> 00:27:02.387
<i>When they see me taking notes,
they come down to study me.</i>

152
00:27:02.705 --> 00:27:05.556
<i>It's like they are the primatologists.</i>

153
00:27:14.633 --> 00:27:18.746
<i>Sifaka don't drink water.</i>

154
00:27:18.846 --> 00:27:21.957
<i>They get all the moisture
they need from fruits...</i>

155
00:27:22.057 --> 00:27:26.411
<i>and the little leaves
between the spines of plants.</i>

156
00:27:31.483 --> 00:27:36.712
<i>I've followed them for 20 years
and they still amaze me.</i>

157
00:27:43.787 --> 00:27:49.559
<i>I teach my students that lemurs
are Madagascar's living treasure.</i>

158
00:27:52.129 --> 00:27:56.784
<i>But what's most amazing
about the sifaka...</i>

159
00:27:56.884 --> 00:28:00.945
<i>is how they dance.</i>

160
00:29:23.345 --> 00:29:25.205
<i>After months of searching...</i>

161
00:29:25.305 --> 00:29:29.668
<i>Patricia's team finally found
a new group of greater bamboo lemurs...</i>

162
00:29:29.768 --> 00:29:33.996
<i>to provide mates for the family
in the national park.</i>

163
00:29:34.898 --> 00:29:40.169
<i>Their habitat is awful,
I mean, very degraded.</i>

164
00:29:40.279 --> 00:29:43.974
I am so relieved. I'm really relieved.
I mean, my goodness...

165
00:29:44.074 --> 00:29:47.552
we have been chasing those animals
for a long time.

166
00:29:48.495 --> 00:29:51.138
<i>We have to catch them today.</i>

167
00:30:10.976 --> 00:30:15.047
<i>When we reached the lemurs,
fires were burning throughout the forest...</i>

168
00:30:15.147 --> 00:30:18.207
<i>and I hoped we weren't too late.</i>

169
00:30:29.453 --> 00:30:32.847
<i>They captured them just in time.</i>

170
00:30:35.667 --> 00:30:40.146
<i>But another piece of forest is gone.</i>

171
00:30:58.232 --> 00:31:02.428
See if she has milk,
or if she's pregnant.

172
00:31:02.528 --> 00:31:04.388
<i>Back at ValBio...</i>

173
00:31:04.488 --> 00:31:07.766
<i>the rescued lemurs
are sedated and examined...</i>

174
00:31:07.866 --> 00:31:11.687
<i>to make sure they are free
from parasites and disease.</i>

175
00:31:11.787 --> 00:31:14.972
The canine has tooth wear. Okay.

176
00:31:17.084 --> 00:31:20.487
<i>The new lemurs wear radio collars...</i>

177
00:31:20.587 --> 00:31:24.607
<i>so scientists can
easily monitor their progress.</i>

178
00:31:30.180 --> 00:31:33.417
<i>I've studied these animals
for so long...</i>

179
00:31:33.517 --> 00:31:36.952
<i>but this is the first time
I've ever held one in my arms.</i>

180
00:31:37.187 --> 00:31:39.914
You're really beautiful.

181
00:31:42.317 --> 00:31:44.511
So amazing.

182
00:31:44.611 --> 00:31:48.223
I thought you guys were extinct. Yeah.

183
00:31:48.323 --> 00:31:50.767
What a shame that would be.

184
00:31:50.867 --> 00:31:54.220
Such beautiful animals.

185
00:31:54.830 --> 00:31:58.808
But now you're going to be
in the national park. Yeah.

186
00:32:00.210 --> 00:32:03.780
<i>Soon after,
Patricia brings the rescued lemurs...</i>

187
00:32:03.880 --> 00:32:06.700
<i>to an enclosure in the rain forest...</i>

188
00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:11.612
<i>so they can get used to the environment
before meeting the residents.</i>

189
00:32:22.899 --> 00:32:25.251
<i>So much was at stake.</i>

190
00:32:26.028 --> 00:32:29.255
<i>But even I didn't know what to expect.</i>

191
00:32:31.700 --> 00:32:33.727
<i>Would they fall in love?</i>

192
00:32:33.827 --> 00:32:35.761
<i>Would they fight?</i>

193
00:32:36.204 --> 00:32:39.056
<i>Would they even find each other?</i>

194
00:32:42.919 --> 00:32:48.575
<i>The next day, the father
and daughter discover the cage...</i>

195
00:32:48.675 --> 00:32:52.879
<i>and realize they are no longer alone.</i>

196
00:34:27.274 --> 00:34:30.751
<i>I didn't expect true love right away.</i>

197
00:34:31.486 --> 00:34:34.547
<i>They have to get to know each other.</i>

198
00:34:45.333 --> 00:34:50.072
<i>But this seems like the start
of a beautiful friendship.</i>

199
00:35:29.836 --> 00:35:35.774
<i>If all goes well, next year
we'll have babies in the park.</i>

200
00:35:39.346 --> 00:35:42.290
<i>That's how we're going
to save these lemurs.</i>

201
00:35:42.390 --> 00:35:45.293
<i>One generation at a time.</i>

202
00:35:53.568 --> 00:35:59.006
<i>Across Madagascar,
lemurs have an uphill battle to survive.</i>

203
00:36:01.827 --> 00:36:06.055
<i>But momentum is shifting in their favor.</i>

204
00:36:07.541 --> 00:36:12.102
<i>Some villagers have begun
to fight fires...</i>

205
00:36:12.337 --> 00:36:14.865
<i>not just start them.</i>

206
00:36:23.723 --> 00:36:26.033
<i>And thanks to people like Hanta...</i>

207
00:36:26.518 --> 00:36:31.131
<i>kids are teaching their elders
about conservation.</i>

208
00:36:31.231 --> 00:36:35.459
<i>And learning to avoid the mistakes
of their ancestors.</i>

209
00:37:17.694 --> 00:37:22.172
<i>Lemurs came to Madagascar as castaways.</i>

210
00:37:27.203 --> 00:37:32.808
<i>Their epic adventure has lasted
for 60 million years.</i>

211
00:37:39.174 --> 00:37:42.693
<i>Fate brought the lemurs to Madagascar.</i>

212
00:37:43.803 --> 00:37:48.157
<i>But they'll need more than luck
to survive much longer.</i>

213
00:37:51.102 --> 00:37:53.162
<i>They'll need help.</i>

214
00:38:10.080 --> 00:38:11.930
<i>Hello.</i>

215
00:38:16.211 --> 00:38:20.014
How are you?
Are you doing okay up there?

216
00:38:21.967 --> 00:38:26.695
<i>The more I get to know lemurs,
the more I love them.</i>

217
00:38:31.810 --> 00:38:36.381
<i>And I want to share these
incredible animals with the world.</i>

218
00:38:38.483 --> 00:38:42.012
<i>Lemurs have a miraculous story.</i>

219
00:38:42.112 --> 00:38:46.090
<i>Now it's up to us to keep it alive.</i>

220
00:38:47.784 --> 00:38:49.519
<i>After all...</i>

221
00:38:49.619 --> 00:38:56.016
<i>the best stories in nature
are the ones that never end.</i>
